-- --opens specification (seg/WRITING.md, rule 6) for DeloopR (doc/cross-term.pdf,
-- Section 6: Theorem 16, Definition 17, Theorem 18, Corollary 19): one entry per
-- declaration, generated from --opened (28 Oct 2026) and checked against the
-- note by kind.  Kinds as in cross.opens; in addition:
--   by-definition steps of the text: Over.C, Over.Rel, Over.Unloop, isContr
--     (the centre of Unloop f is (Fhat, gamma)); Cross.f, Cross.Dp (cell0: the
--     cell at x0 is (w0, |f|, f = D_p)); BR, br0, Fib, fpt, OF, FibSq,
--     FibConn.F, Triple.F, Triple.f0 (the fibres of the text); phi, pt-inv,
--     Acc.inv (phi-def: phi is the section of omega-BR); Torsors.Mu; isTrunc
--     (trunc-Sigma at isTrunc 6);
--   omega-BR is locked after its definition (only used as a pointed
--     equivalence), so phi-def does not open its construction;
--   extras, not steps of the text: K(Z,3) as a type (KK.K -> EMSpace.K ->
--     EMn.Kstage -> Step.next -> Deloop.Torsors.Tor) in rel and BR-trunc, which
--     bind a variable over X = K(Z,3): the etaV defect, as in h4.opens.
-- Check: segd All.seg --opens deloop.opens ; every line "nothing else opened".
